                "text": "**Analyzing Grid Patterns**\n\nOkay, I'm currently focusing on how the 1s and 2s are arranged within the 2x2 blocks of the grid. I've begun to analyze Example 1 and have determined the block location for 1s and 2s, in terms of rows and columns. I'm noting the positions of these blocks and beginning to see how that translates to the output. Specifically, I'm working to link how a block translates to a diagonal line.\n\n\n**Determining Movement Patterns**\n\nOkay, I've confirmed that '1' always generates a diagonal line moving up-left from the top-left corner of its 2x2 block. Now, I'm analyzing the relationship between the positions of '1' and '2'. I see that '2' always generates a diagonal line moving down-right. I'm trying to determine whether '1' and '2' interact, or if the position of the 2 affects the position of the line generated by the 1.\n\n\n**Investigating Line Termination**\n\nOkay, I'm now focused on understanding when the diagonal lines generated by '1' and '2' terminate. I've realized they extend until they hit the grid boundary. Example 3 highlights this: the '2' line stops when it hits the 9th column. Similarly, the '1' line stops when it hits the first column. This is consistent across all examples, it appears the line will continue until the grid border has been reached. I'm now working to confirm this boundary rule is consistent with other examples.\n\n\n",
